## Data Storage Architecture

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The current pipeline stores only `fingerprint_image` (raw pixels) + `fingerprint_template`
> (encrypted minutiae). The v4 matching pipeline registers the sensor probe image against
> the stored enrolled image at match time — so we need the stored enrolled image to be
> the binarised+normalised form, not the raw grayscale.

### What must be stored per enrolled student

To support 1-to-many matching at exam time:

| Field | Content | Size |
|-------|---------|------|
| `fingerprint_image` | Processed binary-normalised image (400×500 uint8) | 200,000 bytes |
| `fingerprint_template` | Encrypted serialised `FingerprintTemplate` (minutiae + singularities) | ~2–5 KB |
| `fingerprint_hash` | SHA-256 of template bytes | 64 bytes |

The `fingerprint_image` stores the **binarised + width-normalised** image (the `b1_norm` in v4
terms), so at match time the sensor probe can be registered directly against it without
re-running the full binarisation pipeline on the stored image.

### DB Migration Required

The `Student.fingerprint_image` field currently has `max_length=262144` (512×512).
New size is 400×500 = 200,000 bytes — fits within existing max_length, but:

- Old enrolled images are 512×512 → cannot be reshaped to 400×500 → **must be cleared**
- A migration will add a `fingerprint_image_size` field to store `(H, W)` for future-proofing,
  and will clear all existing `fingerprint_image` and `fingerprint_template` blobs

```
Migration actions:
  1. Add Student.fingerprint_image_size = CharField(max_length=20, default='400x500')
  2. Clear all existing fingerprint_image / fingerprint_template / fingerprint_hash data
  3. Leave max_length=262144 (still fits 400x500 with headroom)
```

